26 | publisher PDF | [2026_machines_prefer_humans](2026_machines_prefer_humans.pdf) |\n\nAll ten user-specified arXiv PDFs were inspected across every three-page chunk, with text-assisted reading and rendered chunk sheets. Devbunova (2603.19426) also received a complete read. Other discovered papers received abstract/methods screening, not a claimed full appendix review. Detailed evidence: [reading log](../notes/reading_log.md) and [extended notes](../notes/extended_reading.md).\n\nPDF chunks and manifests are in `pages/`; duplicate chunk PDFs are ignored by git. Regenerate with `uv run python scripts/prepare_reading.py`. The LessWrong post is saved as HTML/text in `notes/lesswrong.*`; it summarizes an earlier version of 2505.14617 and is not an independent paper.\n[\n  {\n    \"id\": \"2310.13548\",\n    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2310.13548\",\n    \"title\": [\n      \"Towards Understanding Sycophancy in Language Models\"\n    ],\n    \"author\": [\n      \"Sharma, Mrinank\",\n      \"Tong, Meg\",\n      \"Korbak, Tomasz\",\n      \"Duvenaud, David\",\n      \"Askell, Amanda\",\n      \"Bowman, Samuel R.\",\n      \"Cheng, Newton\",\n      \"Durmus, Esin\",\n      \"Hatfield-Dodds, Zac\",\n      \"Johnston, Scott R.\",\n      \"Kravec, Shauna\",\n      \"Maxwell, Timothy\",\n      \"McCandlish, Sam\",\n      \"Ndousse, Kamal\",\n      \"Rausch, Oliver\",\n      \"Schiefer, Nicholas\",\n      \"Yan, Da\",\n      \"Zhang, Miranda\",\n      \"Perez, Ethan\"\n    ],\n    \"date\": [\n      \"2023/10/20\"\n    ],\n    \"pages\": 35,\n    \"bytes\": 1383108,\n    \"sha256\": \"ee764bd30119f2146f2e130a099d6d313fca6c70ab07b17b7fdbde456d96be36\",\n    \"version\": \"2310.13548v4\",\n    \"local_path\": \"papers/2310.13548.pdf\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"2212.09251\",\n    \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2212.09251\",\n    \"title\": [\n      \"Discovering Language Model Behaviors with Model-Written Evaluations\"\n    ],\n    \"author\": [\n      \"Perez, Ethan\",\n