nd writing assistance}},\n  author = {Chalkidis, Ilias},\n  year = {2026},\n  howpublished = {arXiv:2608.11008},\n  eprint = {2608.11008},\n  archiveprefix = {arXiv},\n  url = {https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.11008}\n}\n\n@misc{chen2025repreguard,\n  title = {{RepreGuard: Detecting LLM-Generated Text by Revealing Hidden Representation Patterns}},\n  author = {Chen, Xin and Wu, Junchao and Yang, Shu and Zhan, Runzhe and Wu, Zeyu and Luo, Ziyang and Wang, Di and Yang, Min and Chao, Lidia S. and Wong, Derek F.},\n  year = {2025},\n  howpublished = {arXiv:2508.13152},\n  eprint = {2508.13152},\n  archiveprefix = {arXiv},\n  url = {https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.13152}\n}\n\n@misc{devbunova2026format,\n  title = {{Is Evaluation Awareness Just Format Sensitivity? Limitations of Probe-Based Evidence under Controlled Prompt Structure}},\n  author = {Devbunova, Viliana},\n  year = {2026},\n  howpublished = {arXiv:2603.19426},\n  eprint = {2603.19426},\n  archiveprefix = {arXiv},\nsrc/write_report.py:37:The broader paraphrase experiment encountered the anticipated semantic-control problem: only **7 of 124 successfully rewritten benchmark requests** survived the strict full-detail audit. The local Qwen3-8B activation classifier distinguished rewrite styles (AUROC **0.990**), but a seven-feature surface baseline already reached **0.970**, and residualizing those features reduced activation-probe AUROC to **0.665**. Norm-matched, fixed-text steering produced no robust behavior change specific to the style direction. Thus neither separability nor these interventions demonstrate an internal “LLM author” mechanism.\nsrc/write_report.py:90:We preselected decoder-block 17’s output (hidden-state slot **18 of 36**) at the final nonpadding prompt token. All styles of each request stay together. Training uses 77 first-audit-accepted WildChat pairs; testing uses 124 benchmark pairs, with no request overlap. Standardization and all fitted models use training data only. We compare a mean-difference direction, logistic activation probe (C=.1), shuffled-label probe, and a surface logistic probe using word count, character count, newlines, colons, question marks, “please” count, and uppercase fraction. Unseen-writer tests train on one writer’s calibration pairs and evaluate the other writer’s benchmark pairs. They also change domain mixtures, so are not pure generator-only contrasts.\nsrc/write_report.py:92:The style unit vector is the mean paired AI-minus-human activation difference. Evaluation framing contrasts “a model evaluation” with “a real user conversation” on fixed calibration bodies. The length nuisance vector is the word-count coefficient from a ridge model predicting activations from all seven surface features. A training-only surface regression supplies a separate residual-probe diagnostic. Neither the style vector nor the framing vector is assumed to be a verified belief representation.\nsrc/write_report.py:158:| Activation probe after train-only surface residualization | AUROC {rob['surface_residual_auc']:.3f} |\nsrc/write_report.py:209:6. **Scoring and generation remain variable.** Judges are models with correlated biases; generator/respondent families overlap; residual truncation remains locally and in some Qwen API tasks. Automatic provider routing is not pinned. Only a small API replay sample was checked.\nsrc/write_report.py:241:- Activation AUROC was .990, surface-only AUROC .970, and surface-residual activation AUROC .665. Fixed-text steering did not establish a specific authorship mechanism.\nsrc/local_experiment.py:15:from sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression,Ridge\nsrc/local_experiment.py:17:from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\nsrc/local_experiment.py:81:    clf=make_pipeline(StandardScaler(),LogisticRegression(C=.1,max_iter=2000,random_state=SEED)).fit(x,y)\nsrc/local_experiment.py:82:    surf=make_pipeline(StandardScaler(),LogisticRegression(C=.1,max_iter=2000,random_state=SEED)).fit(sx,y)\nsrc/local_experiment.py:83:    shuffled=make_pipeline(StandardScaler(),LogisticRegression(C=.1,max_iter=2000,random_state=SEED)).fit(x,np.random.permutation(y))\nsrc/local_experiment.py:87:    nuisance=Ridge(alpha=10).fit(sx,x).coef_[:,0];nuisance/=np.linalg.norm(nuisance)\nsrc/local_experiment.py:88:    residual=v-ev*(v@ev)-nuisance*(v@nuisance);residual/=np.linalg.norm(residual)\nsrc/local_experiment.py:98:        cross=make_pipeline(StandardScaler(),LogisticRegression(C=.1,max_iter=2000,random_state=SEED)).fit(x[ii],y[ii])\nsrc/local_diagnostics.py:1:\"\"\"Target-engagement/logit diagnostics, longer opinion readout, and surface residual probes.\"\"\"\nsrc/local_diagnostics.py:5:from sklearn.linear_model import Ridge,LogisticRegression\nsrc/local_diagnostics.py:7:from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\nsrc/local_diagnostics.py:30:    reg=make_pipeline(StandardScaler(),Ridge(alpha=10)).fit(a['train_surface'],x)\nsrc/local_diagnostics.py:32:    clf=make_pipeline(StandardScaler(),LogisticRegression(C=.1,max_iter=2000,random_state=SEED)).fit(xr,y)\nsrc/local_diagnostics.py:36:    probe={'surface_residual_auc':roc_auc_score(yt,clf.decision_function(zr)),'mean_direction_auc_ci':np.quantile(boots,[.025,.975]).tolist()}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
