{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_31","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > paper_draft/README.md <<'EOF'\n# Manuscript\n\n**Prompt Formatting Shifts Authorship Judgments Without Establishing Behavioral Effects**\n\nAuthors: Dang Nguyen and NeuriCo.\n\nOpen \"'`main.pdf` for the compiled paper or edit `main.tex` and the modular files in `sections/`, `tables/`, and `appendix/`. The project includes two figures, seven tables, and 18 bibliography entries. The PDF has 14 pages: nine main-text pages, two reference pages, and three appendix pages.\n\nCompile from this directory:\n\n```bash\npdflatex -interaction=nonstopmode main.tex\nbibtex main\npdflatex -interaction=nonstopmode main.tex\npdflatex -interaction=nonstopmode main.tex\n```\n\nThe bundled NeurIPS style requires a track name even with the requested `[final]` option. `main.tex` supplies a neutral research-manuscript notice without changing the required style line or claiming conference acceptance. Standard TeX Live packages supply the command-template dependencies. The abstract uses the NeurIPS abstract environment; all body and appendix section files contain their section commands.\n\nAll assets needed to compile are included. To regenerate numerical tables, the vector plot, and bibliography from the original experiment repository, run `python paper_draft/scripts/build_assets.py` from the repository root with matplotlib installed. This optional step requires the parent repository'\"'s saved results and paper catalog; ordinary compilation does not.\n\nThe supplied report is the empirical source. Bibliographic metadata come from its saved paper catalog. Dataset/model/documentation entries use the 2026 study snapshot year and identify that convention explicitly. No new experiments were performed. \"'`REVIEW.md` records the final checks; `OUTLINE.md` maps claims to evidence.\nEOF\ncp paper/OUTLINE.md paper_draft/OUTLINE.md\ncat > paper_draft/REVIEW.md <<'\"'EOF'\n# Final manuscript review\n\n## Resources and style\n\n- Read \"'`.codex/skills/paper-writer/SKILL.md` and `templates/paper_writing/lab_style_guide.md` before drafting.\n- Inspected `paper_examples/`: only a README was supplied; no example sections, tables, or macros were available to browse.\n- Verified and imported all three supplied command templates. Customized project terms; retained shared templates.\n- Used the citation-manager skill and saved catalog metadata; no example content was copied.\n\n## Content and language\n\n- Abstract: 196 whitespace-delimited words (within 150–250).\n- Exact author block: `'\"\\\\author{Dang Nguyen and NeuriCo}\"'`.\n- Introduction follows motivation, gap, approach with figure, quantitative preview, three specific contributions, and roadmap.\n- Related work is organized by awareness, recognition/preference, detection/confounds, and opinion measurement.\n- Main claims remain bounded: generated human style is not verified human provenance; no primary significance does not establish general equivalence; activation discrimination does not establish mediation.\n- Preserved semantic attrition, conditional-choice selection, unconditional Qwen signal with adjusted p=.0781, scoring uncertainty, local truncation, and API replay variability.\n- Distinguished six-test primary correction, two-model opinion sensitivity correction, and exploratory source labels/interventions.\n- Checked intervention scaling and centering formula against implementation. Clarified 2,000 bootstrap draws for probe AUROC versus 10,000 for paired behavior.\n- Numerical behavioral, perception, attrition, label, and intervention tables generated directly from saved CSVs; probe numbers checked against report and saved metrics.\n\n## Formatting and compilation\n\n- Required NeurIPS `[final]` style, hyperref, booktabs, graphicx, amsmath/amssymb, command imports, and plainnat are present.\n- Native LaTeX method diagram and vector statistical figure have self-contained captions; figure labels visually inspected at rendered size.\n- Tables use booktabs without vertical lines. Highest probe AUROC is bold; behavioral extrema are not falsely framed as performance wins.\n- Citation validator: 18 entries, zero errors, zero warnings.\n- Final PDF: 14 pages. Inspected rendered contact sheet and individual title, plot, and appendix pages; fixed an overlapping plot title and awkward appendix spacing.\n- Final LaTeX log: no errors, undefined citations/references, overfull boxes, or rerun warnings. Some harmless underfull-box notices remain.\n- PDF contains clickable citation and cross-reference links.\n- All sections complete; no prose placeholders. Abstract follows the standard unnumbered conference environment.\n\n## Build correction\n\nThe supplied style left `'\"\\\\@trackname\"'` undefined under the required `[final]` option. Added a neutral fallback notice in `main.tex`, preserving the required package line and avoiding an unsupported conference-acceptance implication.\nEOF\n.venv/bin/python .codex/skills/citation-manager/scripts/validate_citations.py paper_draft/references.bib\n.venv/bin/python - <<'\"'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport re, json, zipfile, pymupdf\np=Path('paper_draft')\nfiles=[p/'main.tex',*sorted((p/'sections').glob('*.tex')),*sorted((p/'appendix').glob('*.tex')),*sorted((p/'tables').glob('*.tex')),*sorted((p/'figures').glob('*.tex'))]\ns='\\\\n'.join(x.read_text() for x in files)\nkeys=set(re.findall(r'@\\\\w+\\\\{([\"'^,]+),'\"',(p/'references.bib').read_text()))\ncited={k for group in re.findall(r'\\\\\\\\cite(?:t|p)?(?:\\\\[[\"'^'\"\\\\]]*\\\\])*\\\\{([\"'^}]+)'\"\\\\}',s) for k in group.split(',')}\nassert cited==keys,(cited-keys,keys-cited)\nlog=(p/'main.log').read_text()\nassert not re.search(r'\"'^!|undefined|Overfull|Rerun to get'\"',log,re.M)\nassert r'\\\\author{Dang Nguyen and NeuriCo}' in s\nassert not re.search(r'\\\\b(TODO|TBD|PLACEHOLDER)\\\\b',s)\ndoc=pymupdf.open(p/'main.pdf')\nassert len(doc)==14\nprint(json.dumps({'pages':len(doc),'references':len(keys),'links':sum(len(page.get_links()) for page in doc),'unresolved_citations':0,'compilation_errors':0}))\ninclude=[p/'main.tex',p/'main.pdf',p/'references.bib',p/'neurips_2025.sty',p/'README.md',p/'REVIEW.md',p/'OUTLINE.md']\nfor sub in ['sections','appendix','tables','commands','figures','scripts']:\n    include.extend(x for x in (p/sub).rglob('*') if x.is_file() and '__pycache__' not in x.parts)\nwith zipfile.ZipFile(p/'paper_source.zip','w',zipfile.ZIP_DEFLATED) as z:\n    for f in include:z.write(f,f.relative_to(p.parent))\nprint('Created paper_draft/paper_source.zip')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
